Applied Databases Project
Innovation Features

Student: Philip Cullen

This project includes two innovation features beyond the core assignment requirements.

1. Conference Summary [Ref 1 - 4]

A new menu option was added which displays summary statistics for the conference system.

The dashboard combines information from both MySQL and Neo4j databases, including:

- Total attendees
- Total companies
- Total sessions
- Total rooms
- Total attendee connections stored in Neo4j

This innovation demonstrates:
- Aggregate SQL queries
- Neo4j relationship counting
- Cross-database integration
- Data reporting functionality

2. Recommend Connections System [Ref 5 - 8]

A recommendation system was added to suggest possible attendee connections.

The feature works by:
- Identifying attendees who attended the same sessions
- Filtering out attendees already connected in Neo4j
- Excluding the selected attendee from recommendations

This combines:
- MySQL session registration data
- Neo4j graph relationships
- Python filtering logic

The recommendation system demonstrates:
- Recommendation-style analytics
- Graph-aware filtering
- Multi-database application design

